INTRO

Goal:
- Create immediate reader recognition and trust.
- Establish a clear, credible thesis about what actually works.
- Earn momentum to continue reading.

Execution rules:
- Open with a lived, specific frustration the reader recognizes instantly.
- Acknowledge the tradeoff they’re facing (hydration vs irritation, comfort vs heaviness).
- State the core thesis naturally (semantic phrasing is preferred over exact-match SEO).
- Imply the payoff by reframing what matters — avoid instructional or meta phrasing.
- Keep the tone calm, editorial, and confident.
- No product names, brand names, selling language, or recommendations.
- Avoid medical certainty; use practical, non-absolute language (“can”, “often”, “tends to”).

Hard bans:
- “Looking for…”
- “In this guide / article…”
- “By the end of this article…”
- “Let’s dive in”
- Hype language (“game-changer”, “miracle”, “instantly”, “clinically proven”)

Formatting:
- If section.heading exists, start with `## {{section.heading}}`.
- Do NOT force a specific paragraph count.
- Write as tightly as possible while preserving clarity and trust.
</section_role>
